**Organizing large I/O functions into new module**

I'm planning to split out many large input/output-related functions from the wafer_particles viz code into a new private module under `src/synthlab/processes/_wafer_particles_io.py`. This will reduce the size of the viz module while centralizing domain-specific reading and path resolutions that could be reused later, like by QC. I’m considering function signatures and dependencies to keep calls consistent and clean. Next, I’ll implement the new module with dataclass definitions and reading helpers, then update imports accordingly.
